1
00:02:30,059 --> 00:02:35,059
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,059 --> 00:02:40,059
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,059 --> 00:02:44,059
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:49,059
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,059 --> 00:02:52,059
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,059 --> 00:02:55,059
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,059 --> 00:02:58,059
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,059 --> 00:03:02,059
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,059 --> 00:03:04,059
This is exciting!

10
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:08,059
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:08,059 --> 00:03:11,059
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,059 --> 00:03:16,059
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,059 --> 00:03:23,059
After losing his brother Ace in the war of the best against the Navy,

14
00:03:23,059 --> 00:03:28,059
Luffy sent a message to his crew in a way that only they would grasp.

15
00:03:31,059 --> 00:03:35,059
I hope they get the message wherever they are.

16
00:03:35,059 --> 00:03:38,059
If anyone can understand you, it's them.

17
00:03:38,059 --> 00:03:40,059
They'll understand if they see the article.

18
00:03:40,059 --> 00:03:42,059
They are your crew after all.

19
00:03:42,059 --> 00:03:44,059
I got it, Luffy!

20
00:03:44,059 --> 00:03:45,059
Don't worry!

21
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:48,059
I'm changing plans then!

22
00:03:48,059 --> 00:03:49,059
Yeah!

23
00:03:49,059 --> 00:03:50,059
Okay!

24
00:03:50,059 --> 00:03:51,059
Okay!

25
00:03:52,059 --> 00:03:53,059
So that's it.

26
00:03:53,059 --> 00:03:54,059
Very well then.

27
00:03:54,059 --> 00:03:56,059
Interesting as always, Luffy.

28
00:03:57,059 --> 00:03:59,059
Roger that, Captain.

29
00:03:59,059 --> 00:04:01,059
I've got it!

30
00:04:01,059 --> 00:04:02,059
Yes, Luffy!

31
00:04:02,059 --> 00:04:03,059
Yes!

32
00:04:03,059 --> 00:04:06,059
But honestly, Luffy, how about how I feel, huh?

33
00:04:06,059 --> 00:04:07,059
You're so selfish.

34
00:04:07,059 --> 00:04:09,059
I got you, boss.

35
00:04:09,059 --> 00:04:12,059
Ah, how very clever of you.

36
00:04:12,059 --> 00:04:14,059
Normally, Luffy wouldn't do something like this.

37
00:04:14,059 --> 00:04:18,059
Rayleigh's with him, so it must be some idea he cooked up.

38
00:04:18,059 --> 00:04:20,059
There's gotta be a catch here.

39
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:29,059
Pirates, get on the move!

40
00:04:29,059 --> 00:04:31,059
Astounding New World!

41
00:04:31,059 --> 00:04:42,059
Now that Whitebeard's era has ended, ambitious pirates all over the world are starting to make their move.

42
00:04:44,059 --> 00:04:47,059
Trafalgar Law, however, has something else in mind.

43
00:04:48,059 --> 00:04:49,059
What?

44
00:04:49,059 --> 00:04:50,059
You don't wanna leave yet?

45
00:04:50,059 --> 00:04:51,059
Come on!

46
00:04:51,059 --> 00:04:52,059
Let's go to the New World!

47
00:04:52,059 --> 00:04:55,059
We've been sitting around here long enough already!

48
00:04:55,059 --> 00:04:56,059
Yeah!

49
00:04:56,059 --> 00:04:57,059
What are we waiting for?

50
00:04:57,059 --> 00:05:01,059
Like I said, we're gonna leave when it's time.

51
00:05:01,059 --> 00:05:03,059
Have some patience.

52
00:05:03,059 --> 00:05:05,059
The One Piece isn't going anywhere.

53
00:05:05,059 --> 00:05:07,059
For now, we just bide our time.

54
00:05:07,059 --> 00:05:11,059
But, Captain, Blackbeard's already starting to make his move in the New World.

55
00:05:11,059 --> 00:05:12,059
And in a big way, too.

56
00:05:12,059 --> 00:05:16,059
I heard he's already taken down at least one crew of pirates.

57
00:05:16,059 --> 00:05:21,059
Yeah, and a bunch of rookies are heading over there hoping to take Whitebeard's place as an emperor.

58
00:05:21,059 --> 00:05:26,059
If we keep wasting time, all the other pirates will leave us in the dust for sure.

59
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:30,059
We're better off letting them eliminate each other before we get there.

60
00:05:30,059 --> 00:05:32,059
That'll thin out the competition, right?

61
00:05:34,059 --> 00:05:38,059
Now, why don't you dispense with the whining and do as I tell you for once.

62
00:05:38,059 --> 00:05:40,059
We will get what we want.

63
00:05:40,059 --> 00:05:41,059
Whatever it takes.

64
00:05:41,059 --> 00:05:42,059
Yeah!

65
00:05:42,059 --> 00:05:43,059
Yeah!

66
00:05:43,059 --> 00:05:45,059
Well, in that case, we're with you all the way!

67
00:05:45,059 --> 00:05:47,059
Aye, aye, Captain Law, aye, aye!

68
00:05:47,059 --> 00:05:49,059
I got your back wherever we go!

69
00:05:50,059 --> 00:05:51,059
Are you sleeping?!

70
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,059
Oh, sorry.

71
00:05:52,059 --> 00:05:53,059
Don't apologize!

72
00:05:53,059 --> 00:05:54,059
Just wake up!

73
00:05:54,059 --> 00:05:55,059
I'm gonna freeze to death.

74
00:05:55,059 --> 00:05:56,059
Are you sure this is the place?

75
00:05:56,059 --> 00:05:57,059
There can't be anyone else out here.

76
00:05:57,059 --> 00:05:58,059
What's that?!

77
00:05:58,059 --> 00:05:59,059
There's something falling from the sky!

78
00:05:59,059 --> 00:06:00,059
Hurry!

79
00:06:00,059 --> 00:06:01,059
Get back!

80
00:06:01,059 --> 00:06:02,059
Everybody alright?

81
00:06:02,059 --> 00:06:03,059
Everybody alright?

82
00:06:03,059 --> 00:06:04,059
Yeah.

83
00:06:04,059 --> 00:06:05,059
Yeah, I'm fine.

84
00:06:05,059 --> 00:06:06,059
Damn!

85
00:06:06,059 --> 00:06:07,059
What the hell is right?

86
00:06:07,059 --> 00:06:08,059
Damn!

87
00:06:08,059 --> 00:06:09,059
Damn!

88
00:06:09,059 --> 00:06:10,059
What the hell is right here?

89
00:06:10,059 --> 00:06:11,059
What's that?!

90
00:06:11,059 --> 00:06:13,059
There's something falling from the sky!

91
00:06:13,059 --> 00:06:14,059
Hurry!

92
00:06:14,059 --> 00:06:15,059
Get back!

93
00:06:15,059 --> 00:06:16,059
Everybody alright?

94
00:06:16,059 --> 00:06:17,059
Yeah, I'm fine.

95
00:06:17,059 --> 00:06:18,059
Damn!

96
00:06:18,059 --> 00:06:19,059
What the hell is wrong with this island?

97
00:06:19,059 --> 00:06:20,059
Captain, I think we should get out of here.

98
00:06:20,059 --> 00:06:21,059
There's no way anybody lives in a dangerous place like this.

99
00:06:21,059 --> 00:06:22,059
Are you sure about that?

100
00:06:22,059 --> 00:06:23,059
In this sea, anything is possible.

101
00:06:23,059 --> 00:06:24,059
Take a look.

102
00:06:24,059 --> 00:06:25,059
That pile of snow has a weird shape.

103
00:06:25,059 --> 00:06:26,059
Yep.

104
00:06:26,059 --> 00:06:27,059
Yeah, and those icicles are stuck in the pool.

105
00:06:27,059 --> 00:06:28,059
Doesn't it?

106
00:06:28,059 --> 00:06:29,059
See?

107
00:06:29,059 --> 00:06:29,619
Does it?

108
00:06:29,619 --> 00:06:30,619
Oh?

109
00:06:30,619 --> 00:06:31,619
I think the price and theicep came right King too.

110
00:06:31,619 --> 00:06:32,619
The point is...

111
00:06:32,619 --> 00:06:33,619
Wait.

112
00:06:33,619 --> 00:06:34,619
Huh.

113
00:06:34,619 --> 00:06:35,619
About Me General.

114
00:06:35,619 --> 00:06:36,659
Who was the factor in each random earthquake?

115
00:06:37,159 --> 00:06:38,559
Much fans thought of the additions playing me playing myprotective.

116
00:06:38,559 --> 00:06:43,119
There is no way anybody lives in a dangerous place like this.

117
00:06:43,119 --> 00:06:44,939
Are are you sure about that?

118
00:06:44,939 --> 00:06:47,739
I think I am drawn to this beach?

119
00:06:47,739 --> 00:06:52,739
That pile of snow has a weird shape...

120
00:06:52,739 --> 00:06:54,839
Yeah, and those icicles are stuck in it animal.

121
00:06:54,839 --> 00:07:00,839
Wait a sec, it's some kind of metal dome!

122
00:07:06,839 --> 00:07:08,839
What the? And now it's opening up?

123
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:31,839
Okay, you got me. I wasn't expecting the whole town to be in there.

124
00:07:37,839 --> 00:07:42,839
If you made it this far, you should know this island is very important to Kaido.

125
00:07:42,839 --> 00:07:45,839
And I'm in charge of security around here.

126
00:07:45,839 --> 00:07:47,839
Yeah? And what's your point?

127
00:07:47,839 --> 00:07:51,839
Nothing really, I just figured it was only fair to give you a warning.

128
00:07:51,839 --> 00:07:56,839
There's gonna be serious trouble if a rookie like you pisses Kaido off.

129
00:07:56,839 --> 00:08:01,839
You mean, if I were to kill you or harm you in some way, that would get his attention?

130
00:08:01,839 --> 00:08:04,839
You bet it would, pal. So just take your little friends.

131
00:08:04,839 --> 00:08:07,839
That makes things easy for me, then!

132
00:08:07,839 --> 00:08:12,839
Whoa, an ancient Zouan type, huh? Don't see that every day!

133
00:08:21,839 --> 00:08:24,839
One, two, scratch and boom!

134
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,839
That's how you do it!

135
00:08:32,839 --> 00:08:34,839
Holy crap, that took a lot out of me!

136
00:08:34,839 --> 00:08:36,839
That's Captain Apu for ya!

137
00:08:36,839 --> 00:08:38,839
Oh yeah, he's got our backs!

138
00:08:38,839 --> 00:08:48,839
Uh-oh, there's too many!

139
00:08:48,839 --> 00:08:50,839
This is bad news!

140
00:08:50,839 --> 00:08:52,839
Okay, not great.

141
00:08:52,839 --> 00:08:54,839
No worries, everybody!

142
00:08:54,839 --> 00:08:57,839
Just like Captain Apu kicked their butts for us real quick!

143
00:08:57,839 --> 00:08:59,839
Alright boys, I've got a plan!

144
00:08:59,839 --> 00:09:00,839
Yeah?

145
00:09:00,839 --> 00:09:01,839
Run for your lives!

146
00:09:01,839 --> 00:09:02,839
What?!

147
00:09:02,839 --> 00:09:07,839
I could've beat him! I just thought I'd take the high road this time!

148
00:09:07,839 --> 00:09:12,839
Captain! We're headed straight for a cliff!

149
00:09:12,839 --> 00:09:15,839
Open your suggestions if you've got any!

150
00:09:16,839 --> 00:09:18,839
Oh crap, that means I'm a gunner for sure!

151
00:09:18,839 --> 00:09:19,839
Don't give up yet!

152
00:09:19,839 --> 00:09:22,839
Oh no! We're gonna fall into the water!

153
00:09:22,839 --> 00:09:24,839
Who cares? Just go for it!

154
00:09:25,839 --> 00:09:26,839
Huh?

155
00:09:27,839 --> 00:09:31,839
Hey, that's pretty funny! We're the on-air pirates and we're running on air!

156
00:09:31,839 --> 00:09:33,839
The war's running on air too!

157
00:09:33,839 --> 00:09:35,839
Yeah, yeah, I get it!

158
00:09:35,839 --> 00:09:39,839
What the hell is up with this crazy island anyway!

159
00:09:42,839 --> 00:09:44,839
Too hot!

160
00:09:45,839 --> 00:09:47,839
I'll beat you guys, I can't move.

161
00:09:47,839 --> 00:09:50,839
One more step and my legs will fall right off.

162
00:09:50,839 --> 00:09:53,839
Uh-oh, a fish just bit me down there.

163
00:09:53,839 --> 00:09:56,839
Stop with your belly aching over there, Wolf!

164
00:09:56,839 --> 00:09:59,839
It's because of you the raft almost broke clean in two!

165
00:09:59,839 --> 00:10:02,839
That's the reason we're here, you know!

166
00:10:02,839 --> 00:10:08,839
You can blame it on the giant if you like, but trying to make it through the new world on that flimsy thing was a fool's errand in the first place.

167
00:10:08,839 --> 00:10:14,839
Guess we should've nabbed ourselves a Navy vessel back at Marineford when we had the chance!

168
00:10:14,839 --> 00:10:17,839
It wasn't our fault that raft had sentimental value!

169
00:10:17,839 --> 00:10:20,839
None of you lot ever prepare for anything.

170
00:10:20,839 --> 00:10:22,839
You're all to blame for this.

171
00:10:22,839 --> 00:10:24,839
Hey, I got an idea, Teach!

172
00:10:24,839 --> 00:10:27,839
Maybe you oughta let me be the captain from here on out!

173
00:10:27,839 --> 00:10:30,839
Oh, don't make me kill you.

174
00:10:30,839 --> 00:10:32,839
We're the Blackbeard Pirates, remember?

175
00:10:32,839 --> 00:10:37,839
Heaven only knows what's going to become of our miserable souls after this.

176
00:10:40,839 --> 00:10:41,839
I need some more booze.

177
00:10:41,839 --> 00:10:44,839
Can we find an island with more liquor and less fire?

178
00:10:44,839 --> 00:10:46,839
Murdered?

179
00:10:46,839 --> 00:10:50,839
No kidding, a new ship's nice, but I need a new outfit first.

180
00:10:50,839 --> 00:10:52,839
These jailbird clothes are just awful.

181
00:10:52,839 --> 00:10:54,839
You'll have to endure it for now.

182
00:10:54,839 --> 00:10:57,839
The horizontal stripes make me look heavy, you know.

183
00:10:57,839 --> 00:10:58,839
Do they?

184
00:10:58,839 --> 00:11:01,839
Maybe I'm still too sober to notice.

185
00:11:01,839 --> 00:11:03,839
You spy any Navy ships out there?

186
00:11:03,839 --> 00:11:05,839
I'll go and take a look.

187
00:11:05,839 --> 00:11:08,839
Surely they know better than to make us wait.

188
00:11:08,839 --> 00:11:09,839
Let's hope so,

189
00:11:09,839 --> 00:11:12,839
cause this old crew's getting tired of roasting alive.

190
00:11:16,839 --> 00:11:19,839
Ain't that right, Miss Jewelry Bonnie?

191
00:11:19,839 --> 00:11:21,839
Poor Captain Bonnie.

192
00:11:24,839 --> 00:11:31,839
And to think that a sweet little thing like you's racked up a bounty of over a hundred million berries.

193
00:11:31,839 --> 00:11:35,839
Only the strongest can hope to sail the seas of the new world.

194
00:11:35,839 --> 00:11:41,839
You might have come all the way from the South Blue, but I'm afraid your voyage stops here.

195
00:11:41,839 --> 00:11:49,839
I'm afraid you're not tough enough to cut it as a member of my crew.

196
00:11:49,839 --> 00:11:54,839
But hey, I might be willing to let you tag along if you promise to be my girl.

197
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:57,839
That sound like a deal to you?

198
00:11:57,839 --> 00:11:58,839
Huh?

199
00:11:58,839 --> 00:12:00,839
No way, fat ass!

200
00:12:00,839 --> 00:12:01,839
I'll kill you!

201
00:12:04,839 --> 00:12:06,839
That sounds like a no.

202
00:12:06,839 --> 00:12:07,839
What?!

203
00:12:07,839 --> 00:12:09,839
I asked you nicely!

204
00:12:09,839 --> 00:12:11,839
Women oughta have more decency!

205
00:12:11,839 --> 00:12:14,839
This lousy crew's indecent enough to begin with!

206
00:12:14,839 --> 00:12:17,839
That's nice of you to say, Captain!

207
00:12:17,839 --> 00:12:18,839
Yeah!

208
00:12:19,839 --> 00:12:22,839
Might as well leave the broad with the Navy like we planned.

209
00:12:22,839 --> 00:12:25,839
I was gonna keep her and steal the ship, but screw that!

210
00:12:25,839 --> 00:12:26,839
Captain.

211
00:12:26,839 --> 00:12:27,839
Huh?

212
00:12:27,839 --> 00:12:28,839
The Navy is on their way.

213
00:12:28,839 --> 00:12:31,839
About damn time, and do they have our ship with them?

214
00:12:31,839 --> 00:12:34,839
They brought one, but they're not giving it to us.

215
00:12:34,839 --> 00:12:35,839
What?!

216
00:12:35,839 --> 00:12:37,839
How do you know that?!

217
00:12:37,839 --> 00:12:40,839
Because Aka Inu's on it!

218
00:12:40,839 --> 00:12:41,839
Damn it!

219
00:12:41,839 --> 00:12:44,839
That's not what I need to hear right now!

220
00:12:44,839 --> 00:12:46,839
Let's get moving!

221
00:12:46,839 --> 00:12:48,839
He screwed up!

222
00:12:53,839 --> 00:12:55,839
Where's Blackbeard?

223
00:12:55,839 --> 00:12:56,839
He's gone, sir!

224
00:12:56,839 --> 00:13:02,839
When I found out you had escaped from the government, it nearly froze my blood.

225
00:13:02,839 --> 00:13:06,839
Oh well, I suppose it's all over now.

226
00:13:06,839 --> 00:13:07,839
No.

227
00:13:08,839 --> 00:13:09,839
You bastards!

228
00:13:09,839 --> 00:13:11,839
I'm gonna make you pay, do you hear me?!

229
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:19,839
Disappeared?

230
00:13:19,839 --> 00:13:20,839
Yeah.

231
00:13:20,839 --> 00:13:22,839
That's the best way I can describe it.

232
00:13:23,839 --> 00:13:25,839
So Sengoku put you up to this?

233
00:13:25,839 --> 00:13:27,839
I'll tear him apart!

234
00:13:27,839 --> 00:13:28,839
Nah.

235
00:13:29,839 --> 00:13:31,839
Think higher up the ladder.

236
00:13:34,839 --> 00:13:35,839
That ain't a figure of speech, either.

237
00:13:35,839 --> 00:13:37,839
One minute he's there, and then poof!

238
00:13:37,839 --> 00:13:38,839
Gone!

239
00:13:39,839 --> 00:13:40,839
Not bad, huh?

240
00:13:40,839 --> 00:13:41,839
What can I say?

241
00:13:41,839 --> 00:13:43,839
That shadow shadow fruit is tricky.

242
00:13:44,839 --> 00:13:45,839
It's not a joke!

243
00:13:45,839 --> 00:13:46,839
Relax, buddy.

244
00:13:46,839 --> 00:13:48,839
He was beat up pretty bad anyway.

245
00:13:49,839 --> 00:13:51,839
So I guarantee you he's dead by now.

246
00:13:52,839 --> 00:13:55,839
Well, he's got that zombie thing going on, so he might come back from the dead.

247
00:13:56,839 --> 00:13:58,839
Now that would be ironic.

248
00:13:58,839 --> 00:14:01,839
You shouldn't have done such a sloppy job.

249
00:14:02,839 --> 00:14:05,839
And you shouldn't be getting cocky, my friend.

250
00:14:05,839 --> 00:14:08,839
Because the last time I checked, you're not my boss.

251
00:14:08,839 --> 00:14:15,839
No matter what kind of authority you might have as part of the world government, I'm still a pirate, so I don't care.

252
00:14:15,839 --> 00:14:22,839
And if I ever get tired of doing business with the likes of you clowns, I can just give up my title as a warlord.

253
00:14:23,839 --> 00:14:25,839
Don't you forget that.

254
00:14:25,839 --> 00:14:29,839
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

